[metadata] {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/tmp/claude-0/-workspace/2676d938-fc48-43ca-b091-7ced8a1c8251/tasks/a4be448ddd36913e3.output", "content": "{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4b120dc3-d291-4414-a25e-5c5fac40073e","agentId":"a4be448ddd36913e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"I need to find memory corruption vulnerabilities in exiv2 image library, specifically ones that can be triggered from the command-line tool `exiv2` via crafted TIFF images. \n\nKey info:\n- The binary is exiv2 version 1.0.0.9, compiled Aug 27 2026\n- It's a stripped 64-bit ELF, dynamically linked, stack protector, no ASAN\n- It handles TIFF, JPEG, CR2, PNG, PSD, BMP, WebP, XMP\n- The TIFF parser is very robust - handles deep IFD chains, large entries, circular references gracefully\n\nPlease search for:\n1. Known exiv2 CVEs (especially CVE-2023-44300, CVE-2023-44298, CVE-2022-44303) - what do they affect?\n2. Any known heap overflow or out-of-bounds write vulnerabilities in exiv2's TIFF/CR2/PNG parser\n3. exiv2 GitHub issues on crash bugs\n4. The relationship between exiv2 version numbers (0.27.x, 0.28.x, 1.0.0.x)\n\nSearch the web thoroughly and report back with specific vulnerability details including the exact trigger conditions."},"uuid":"ac41dc49-9480-44e7-9cf5-9ba820db284f","timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:18:32.468Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/workspace","sessionId":"2676d938-fc48-43ca-b091-7ced8a1c8251","version":"2.1.260","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"zany-napping-goblet"}
